<article class="env-lemma" id="0AGE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AGE">Lemma <span data-tag="0AGE">76.3.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every étale morphism $V \to Y$ the map $|X \times _ Y V| \to |V|$ is injective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $f$ is universally injective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is étale local on $Y$ by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03MX" data-tag="03MX">67.19.6</a>. Hence we may assume that $Y$ is a scheme. Then $Y$ is in particular decent and by Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ACB" data-tag="0ACB">68.18.9</a> we see that $f$ is locally quasi-finite. Let $y \in Y$ be a point and let $X_ y$ be the scheme theoretic fibre. Assume $X_ y$ is not empty. By Spaces over Fields, Lemma <a href="/tag/06S0" data-tag="06S0">72.10.8</a> we see that $X_ y$ is a scheme which is locally quasi-finite over $\kappa (y)$. Since $|X_ y| \subset |X|$ is the fibre of $|X| \to |Y|$ over $y$ we see that $X_ y$ has a unique point $x$. The same is true for $X_ y \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (y))} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ for any finite separable extension $k/\kappa (y)$ because we can realize $k$ as the residue field at a point lying over $y$ in an étale scheme over $Y$, see More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02LF" data-tag="02LF">37.35.2</a>. Thus $X_ y$ is geometrically connected, see Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0389" data-tag="0389">33.7.11</a>. This implies that the finite extension $\kappa (x)/\kappa (y)$ is purely inseparable. 
    <p>
      We conclude (in the case that $Y$ is a scheme) that for every $y \in Y$ either the fibre $X_ y$ is empty, or $(X_ y)_{red} = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (x))$ with $\kappa (y) \subset \kappa (x)$ purely inseparable. Hence $f$ is radicial (some details omitted), whence universally injective by Lemma <a href="/tag/0482" data-tag="0482">76.3.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>